{
 "id": "l28",
 "label": "28",
 "title": "Telling time",
 "summary": "Anóng oras na? The hours with ika-, their Spanish equivalents, and words for past, present and future",
 "minutes": 35,
 "goals": [
  "Ask the time with Anóng oras na?",
  "Learn the basic time words: umaga, tangháli, hápon, gabí, oras, minuto…",
  "Tell the hour with ika- + number, and know the Spanish way",
  "Read the short forms n.u., n.t., n.h. and n.g.",
  "Answer kailán questions with words for the present, past and future"
 ],
 "sections": [
  {
   "title": "Anóng oras na?",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "p",
     "t": "Tagalogs love to ask the time. You will often hear strangers ask **Anóng oras na?** (*What time is it?*). Knowing how to tell the time lets you answer in the asker's own language."
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "t": "The book asks you to **memorize** these basic words and phrases. Some of them you already met in Lesson 3."
    },
    {
     "type": "table",
     "head": [
      "Tagalog",
      "Meaning"
     ],
     "rows": [
      [
       "[[umaga|noun]]",
       "morning"
      ],
      [
       "[[tangháli|noun]]",
       "noon (basically 11 a.m. to 1 p.m.)"
      ],
      [
       "[[hápon|noun]]",
       "afternoon"
      ],
      [
       "[[gabí|noun]]",
       "night"
      ],
      [
       "[[hátinggabí|noun]]",
       "midnight"
      ],
      [
       "[[oras|noun]]",
       "hour"
      ],
      [
       "[[kalahatí|noun]]",
       "half"
      ],
      [
       "[[minuto|noun]]",
       "minute"
      ],
      [
       "[[beses|noun]]",
       "frequency"
      ],
      [
       "[[ilang beses|other]]",
       "few times"
      ],
      [
       "[[hanggáng|other]]",
       "until"
      ],
      [
       "[[madalíng-áraw|noun]]",
       "dawn"
      ],
      [
       "[[sandalî|noun]]",
       "second, moment (as a response, it means *for a while*)"
      ]
     ],
     "title": "Basic time words",
     "note": "Lesson 3 wrote umága and tanghálì, and Lesson 13 wrote kalahatì. This lesson prints them as shown here."
    },
    {
     "type": "h",
     "t": "From… until…"
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "t": "**Mulâ** … **hanggáng** gives *from … until*. The book shows one phrase for the present or future and one for the past:"
    },
    {
