  {
   "title": "Telling the hour",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "p",
     "t": "To tell the time in Tagalog, the prefix **ika-** is placed before the **cardinal numbers** (the counting numbers from Lesson 13)."
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "t": "The **Spanish** way of telling time (written in Tagalog spelling) is shown next to it, because it is still very widely used, by Tagalogs and non-Tagalogs alike."
    },
    {
     "type": "box",
     "kind": "tip",
     "title": "One o'clock is different",
     "t": "For one o'clock the book uses **unang oras** (*first hour*): **unang oras ng umaga** is 1:00 a.m. and **únang oras ng hápon** is 1:00 p.m. The Spanish also uses **a la una** (not a las)."
    },
    {
     "type": "table",
     "head": [
      "English",
      "Tagalog",
      "Spanish"
     ],
     "rows": [
      [
       "1:00 a.m.",
       "unang oras ng umaga",
       "a la una ng umaga"
      ],
      [
       "2:00 a.m.",
       "ikalawá ng umaga",
       "a las dos ng umaga"
      ],
      [
       "3:00 a.m.",
       "ikatló ng umaga",
       "a las tres ng umaga"
      ],
      [
       "4:00 a.m.",
       "ika-ápat ng umaga",
       "a las kuwatro ng umaga"
      ],
      [
       "5:00 a.m.",
       "ikalimá ng umaga",
       "a las sinko ng umaga"
      ],
      [
       "6:00 a.m.",
       "ikaánim ng umaga",
       "a las seis ng umaga"
      ],
      [
       "7:00 a.m.",
       "ikapitó ng umaga",
       "a las siyete ng umaga"
      ],
      [
       "8:00 a.m.",
       "ikawaló ng umaga",
       "a las otso ng umaga"
      ],
      [
       "9:00 a.m.",
       "ikasiyám ng umaga",
       "a las nuwebe ng umaga"
      ],
      [
       "10:00 a.m.",
       "ikasampû ng umaga",
       "a las diyes ng umaga"
      ],
      [
       "11:00 a.m.",
       "ikalabing-isá ng umaga",
       "a las onse ng umaga"
      ],
      [
       "12:00 nn",
       "ikalabindalawá ng tánghali",
       "a las dose ng tánghali"
      ]
     ],
     "title": "Morning to noon"
    },
    {
     "type": "table",
     "head": [
      "English",
      "Tagalog",
      "Spanish"
     ],
     "rows": [
      [
       "1:00 p.m.",
       "únang oras ng hápon",
       "a la una ng hápon"
      ],
      [
       "2:00 p.m.",
       "ikalawá ng hápon",
       "a las dos ng hápon"
      ],
      [
       "3:30 p.m.",
       "ikatló at kalahatí ng hápon",
       "a las tres y medya ng hápon"
      ],
      [
       "4:00 p.m.*",
       "ika-ápat ng hápon",
       "a las kuwatro ng hápon"
      ],
      [
       "5:15 p.m.",
       "ikalimá at labinlimang minuto ng hápon",
       "a las sinko y kuwarto ng hápon"
      ],
      [
       "6:40 p.m.",
       "ikaánim at apatnápung minuto ng gabí",
       "a las seis kuwarenta ng gabí"
      ],
      [
       "7:00 p.m.",
       "ikapitó ng gabí",
       "a las siyete ng gabí"
      ],
      [
       "8:00 p.m.",
       "ikawaló ng gabí",
       "a las otso ng gabí"
      ],
      [
       "9:10 p.m.",
       "ikasiyám at sampúng minuto ng gabí",
       "a las nuwebe diyes ng gabí"
      ],
      [
       "10:00 p.m.",
       "ikasampû ng gabí",
       "a las diyes ng gabí"
      ],
      [
       "11:00 p.m.",
       "ikalabíng-isá ng gabí",
       "a las onse ng gabí"
      ],
      [
       "12:00 midnight",
       "ikalabíndalawá ng hátinggabí",
       "a las dose ng hátinggabí"
      ]
     ],
     "title": "Afternoon to midnight",
     "note": "*The book prints \"4:00 a.m.\" on this row, but the row says ng hápon (in the afternoon), so it is 4:00 p.m. The book writes ikalabing-isá / ikalabindalawá in the morning rows and ikalabíng-isá / ikalabíndalawá in the evening rows; it also writes tánghali here and tangháli elsewhere."
    },
    {
     "type": "box",
     "kind": "tip",
     "title": "Reading the table",
     "items": [
      "The hour comes first, then **ng umaga**, **ng tánghali**, **ng hápon** or **ng gabí** for the part of the day.",
      "Minutes are joined with **at** (and): ikalimá **at** labinlimang minuto (5:15), ikasiyám **at** sampúng minuto (9:10).",
      "Half past uses **at kalahatí**: ikatló at kalahatí ng hápon (3:30). The Spanish says **y medya**.",
      "In the table, 5:15 is still ng hápon, while 6:40 is already ng gabí."
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "h",
     "t": "Short forms"
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "t": "The shortened forms of time are the most common in **writing**:"
    },
    {
     "type": "table",
     "head": [
      "Short form",
      "Stands for",
      "Meaning"
     ],
     "rows": [
      [
       "n.u.",
       "ng umaga",
       "a.m."
      ],
      [
       "n.t.",
       "ng tangháli",
       "noon"
      ],
      [
       "n.h.",
       "ng hápon",
       "p.m."
      ],
      [
       "n.g.",
       "ng gabí",
       "evening"
      ]
     ],
     "title": "n.u., n.t., n.h., n.g."
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "t": "The book writes times like this: **ika-7:00 n.g.** You read it aloud as **ikapitó ng gabí**."
    }
   ]
