  {
   "title": "Kailán? Present, past and future",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "p",
     "t": "Lesson 9 introduced **kailán** (*when*) as a question word. Kailán questions ask what time something happened, happens or will happen, or what time someone did, does or will do something."
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "t": "You can answer them with the words and phrases below. Each group (present, past and future) has its **own** words for time. These words can also be joined to dates to give a specific time:"
    },
    {
     "type": "table",
     "head": [
      "Word",
      "Made from",
      "Group"
     ],
     "rows": [
      [
       "[[ngayón|other]]",
       "",
       "present"
      ],
      [
       "[[noóng|other]]",
       "noón + ligature -g",
       "past"
      ],
      [
       "[[kaninang|other]]",
       "kanina + ligature -ng",
       "past"
      ],
      [
       "[[sa|marker]] or [[sa isáng|other]]",
       "isá + ligature -ng",
       "future"
      ],
      [
       "[[sa susunod na|other]]",
       "",
       "future"
      ]
     ],
     "title": "Words that attach to dates",
     "note": "The book writes kanínang and susunód in the lists below."
